{"id":"project-data-pipeline","kind":"project","title":"Data Pipeline","color":"#7b8cff","description":"Portfolio project: API → S3 → warehouse → dbt → dashboard, orchestrated, tested and documented.","lessons":[["git-ci","Git workflow and CI for data"],["docker","Docker-ize the stack"],["dashboard","Serve: a dashboard on your marts"],["failures","Failure scenarios: late data, duplicates, schema changes"],["ship","Ship: the end-to-end pipeline"],["review","Review + quiz","review"]],"quiz":[["What should CI run on every pull request for a data project?",["Nothing","Linting, unit tests and dbt build/tests","Production deploy only","A backup"],1,"CI catches broken models before they reach production."],["A good pipeline README includes…",["Only the license","Architecture, how to run it, and how failures are handled","Your CV","Passwords"],1,"Interviewers read the README to judge your thinking."],["Late-arriving data is best handled by…",["Ignoring it","Reprocessing a window of recent days on each run","Deleting it","Manual fixes"],1,"A sliding reprocess window catches late events."],["A source adds a new column. A robust pipeline…",["Crashes silently","Detects the schema change and alerts or adapts per the contract","Drops the table","Ignores all columns"],1,"Schema drift must be caught, not discovered by users."],["Docker helps a data project because…",["It makes SQL faster","Everyone runs the same environment with one command","It replaces Airflow","It stores data"],1,"Reproducible environments remove 'works on my machine'."]]}
